8461936,2024-03-03,Debt collection,I do not know,Written notification about debt,Didn't receive enough information to verify debt,"To whom it may concern, I am writing to formally dispute the debt appearing on my credit report, as reported by this company. Upon reviewing the information, I have identified several inaccuracies that not only violate fair credit reporting practices but also contravene the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). 

Fluctuating Debt Amount : The reported debt amount has been inconsistently changing without proper validation or justification, a clear violation of FCRA Section 611 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( B ). 
Billing Address Inaccuracy : The billing address associated with the debt ( XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX, NJ XXXX ) is not accurate, infringing upon the FCRA Section 623 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ).

Failure to Provide Licensing Information : The failure to provide licensing information, specifically the NMLS number, is a violation of FCRA Section 605 ( c ) ( 2 ). 
Incomplete Debt Validation : The incomplete debt validation provided violates the FCRA Section 611 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ), requiring detailed information about the original creditor, the account number, the amount owed, the legal basis for claiming I owe the current amount, and the age of the debt.

