8574344,2024-03-18,Checking or savings account,Savings account,Problem with a lender or other company charging your account,Transaction was not authorized,"On XX/XX/XXXX, I opened a Navy Federal checking account and saving account for myself. Approximately a year later on XX/XX/XXXX I opened savings accounts for my three children all of which were XXXX at the time. On XX/XX/XXXX I opened a checking account for my XXXX XXXX XXXX daughter and on XX/XX/XXXX I opened a checking account for my XXXX XXXX XXXX daughter. In XXXX my adult son opened a checking account on his own. During my tenure with Navy Federal I have been granted an auto loan and a credit card both of which were closed/paid in full and remained in good standing and a personal loan that I am currently paying which is in good standing. 

On XX/XX/XXXX, while performing the daily task of checking my Navy Federal bank accounts I was shocked to discover that my checking account balance of {$730.00} and my savings account balance of {$5000.00} were both totally depleted, and the savings account for my son had a balance of - {$37000.00}. I immediately contacted Navy Federal thinking it was a glitch or terrible mistake only to begin what was turn out to be weeks of stress, frustration, and confusion. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Status : Call Disconnected by Rep During my initial call and in a panicked state I tried to explain what was going on to the representative. She told me that there was a check deposited and cashed against my sons checking account that was returned and our accounts are joint, so the funds were taken from my account. I was confused because I know I dont have a joint checking account with my son and never authorized such an account. During this call I alerted my son ( who was home at the time ) of what was going on. During this call of back-and-forth dialogue between myself and the representative with me attempting to explain what I saw in my accounts and her telling me my money would not be returned there was an abrupt ending to the call when the representative disconnected the call while I was still speaking. 

XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Call Disconnected by Rep After the first failed attempt I immediately called back. Instantly upon the representative answering the call I was asked the reason for my call. When I told the representative I had just spoken with someone and they disconnected the call and I was calling back regarding a fraud incident he immediately said, Youre not getting your money back. I then stated, No, this is about a fraudulent check that was deposited into my sons account and you all took the money from my account. He then said again, Youre not getting your money back. I then said to him that he didnt let me explain and I referred him back to my last call and what I was trying to explain to her before she hung up and he said to me, Yes, I see her notes she said you were talking over her. I then told him that I was trying to explain what was going on and he proceeded to tell me why she hung up on me. This led to dialogue between him and I in which I stated that was rude and shouldnt happen in customer service. This became the topic of the dialogue as he continually gave me reasons of why she was valid in hanging up on me and he then disconnected my call. After these two unsuccessful attempts of speaking to someone to gain clarity in this matter I had to stop work, and my son and I went to the XXXX location to speak with someone in person. 

