8578936,2024-03-19,Debt collection,I do not know,Attempts to collect debt not owed,Debt was paid,"On Monday, XX/XX/XXXX, while in XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX, XXXX, I attempted to use my Capital One debit card to make a breakfast purchase. I found that my card was not working. I then checked my account to see three ( 3 ) negative amounts in all three ( 3 ) of my Capital One banking accounts : Simply Checking, Savings Now, and 360 Performance Savings. Because I had received no notification of this occurrence, I was caught completely off guard, especially with being in another country. 

I immediately called Capital One ( XXXX XXXXXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXXXXX ) to seek an explanation of why all of my accounts were in the negative. The Capital One representative explained that my accounts were placed on hold due to a bank levy from the Louisiana Department of Revenue. I was completely shocked as I had received XXXX ( XXXX ) communications from the Department of Revenue as well as Capital One that this would occur. The Capital One representative also explained that once I took care of the financial situation with the Revenue department, they would send Capital One a fax stating I was in the clear, and then within one to two ( 1-2 ) days, I would have access to my accounts again. 

