8653152,2024-03-29,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Subject : Dispute of Bankruptcy Court Statement on Credit Report To Whom It May Concern : I am writing to dispute a statement that has appeared on my credit report from the United States Bankruptcy Court. The statement reads : "" The United States Bankruptcy Court does not report any information to the credit bureaus and is not responsible for verifying or validating information from consumers ' credit files. Bankruptcy filings are publicly available records. '' While bankruptcy filings may be publicly available records, including this statement on my credit report violates my rights to privacy under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ). 

The FCRA prohibits the inclusion of information on a consumer credit report that does not bear directly upon the consumer 's creditworthiness or credit standing. 15 U.S. Code 1681c specifically states that consumer reporting agencies may not disclose bankruptcy case records after 10 years, as they are no longer relevant to credit decisions. 

